  {
    "category": "Numbers",
    "numberBlock": "Regulation 13(2) 'Failure to submit information' provides that: 'if after the measures set out in subsection (1) above, the licensee still fails to submit the information requested, the Authority will deal with the matter in terms of section 114, 115 and 116 of the Act.' Telecom proposes that for the sake of transparency, the penalty for failure to submit information upon request by the Authority be explicitly contained in the Regulations as opposed to making reference to sections in the Communications Act. The thus propose that the process to be followed can be in terms of section 114 and 115.",
    "licensee": "CRAN has harmonised the Penalty framework as the recently published in Penalty Regulations Gazette No. 7197 Notice No. 159. For clarity, we will add a sub-clause to regulation 13 which cross-refers to those regulations, in addition to the general powers of enforcement set out in sections 114-116.",
    "allocationDate": "CRAN has harmonised the Penalty framework as the recently published in Penalty Regulations Gazette No. 7197 Notice No. 159. For clarity, we will add a sub-clause to regulation 13 which cross-refers to those regulations, in addition to the general powers of enforcement set out in sections 114-116.",
    "gazetteRef": "7289"
  },
  {
    "category": "Numbers",
    "numberBlock": "Regulation 12 'Condonation' states that 'All licensees must upload via the data portal statistics on its information and communication technologies complying with the data requirements in Annexure' Telecom proposes that the Authority should ensure that the portal is updated with all its fields.",
    "licensee": "Due to all data submission requirements being incorporated in the portal, some of the fields are not yet fully functional. The portal will be 100% functional before the next data collection period which would be 31 August 2020.",
    "allocationDate": "Due to all data submission requirements being incorporated in the portal, some of the fields are not yet fully functional. The portal will be 100% functional before the next data collection period which would be 31 August 2020.",
    "gazetteRef": "7289"
  },
